---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
const libraries = projects.filter(project => project.kind === 'library');
const buildGuides = [
  { name: 'Activities', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-lib-activities/blob/v0.4.4/README.md#build-and-check', description: 'Provider helpers, portable native code and the shared activity contract.' },
  { name: 'Core', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-lib-core/blob/v0.5.1/README.md#build-and-test', description: 'Reading state, transport helpers and host integration.' },
  { name: 'Dynamic', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-watchface-dynamic/blob/v0.16.2/README.md#build-and-install', description: 'A watchface consuming both shared libraries.' },
  { name: 'Dashboard', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-app-dashboard/blob/v0.4.3/README.md#build-and-validate', description: 'An interactive activity host with pinned readings and actions.' },
  { name: 'Timer', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-app-timer/blob/v0.12.0/README.md#build-and-check', description: 'A native countdown owner with a bundled activity provider.' },
  { name: 'Open Activity', href: 'https://github.com/xefensor/pebble-app-open-activity/blob/v0.1.6/README.md#development-and-validation', description: 'Quick Launch handoff using Dynamic’s recent app destinations.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="For developers" description="Build activity providers and integrate XOCE’s Pebble libraries. Find current API introductions, build instructions and contribution links.">
  <main id="main" class="wrap section page-main">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">For developers</p>
      <h1>Build with the collection.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Publish an activity for compatible hosts, add shared readings to a watchface, or contribute to one of the existing Pebble projects.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-grid">
      <a class="guide-card" href="/docs/develop/activities/"><Icon name="code" size={28} /><h3>Publish an activity</h3><p>Send standard or media content, clocks, an app destination and supported actions. Start with a concrete provider example.</p><span>Activities guide <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></span></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/docs/develop/core/"><Icon name="grid" size={28} /><h3>Integrate readings</h3><p>Use Core’s reading state and transport while your watchface keeps control of its lifecycle and rendering.</p><span>Core guide <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></span></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/design/"><Icon name="spark" size={28} /><h3>Understand the design</h3><p>Read the established principles, current interface patterns and Pebble interaction guidance.</p><span>Design documentation <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></span></a>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout"><Icon name="book" size={25} /><div><h2>Content, presentation and actions have separate owners.</h2><p>Providers supply meaning and supported capabilities. Each host chooses its layout, priority and controls. Dynamic displays activities and app destinations; Dashboard can execute the controls its source binding supports. Timer’s Dashboard Pause/Resume remains unimplemented. <a href="/docs/develop/activities/#app-opening-and-actions">Read the action boundaries.</a></p></div></aside>

    <section class="section" id="libraries" aria-labelledby="developer-libraries">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Embedded dependencies</p><h2 id="developer-libraries">The shared libraries.</h2></div><div class="section-intro"><p>Bundle a pinned version into your app or plugin. Users install the consuming app; these are not separate watch services.</p></div></div>
      <div class="project-grid">{libraries.map(project => <ProjectCard project={project} />)}</div>
    </section>

    <section id="build" aria-labelledby="build-guides">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Work with the source</p><h2 id="build-guides">Build & test.</h2></div><div class="section-intro"><p>Each repository owns its build instructions, SDK requirements and checks. These references match the versions currently listed on this website.</p></div></div>
      <div class="docs-index-grid build-guides">
        <section class="docs-index-group"><h3>Libraries</h3>{buildGuides.slice(0, 2).map(guide => <a href={guide.href}><div><h4>{guide.name}</h4><p>{guide.description}</p></div><Icon name="external" size={17} /></a>)}</section>
        <section class="docs-index-group"><h3>Apps & watchface</h3>{buildGuides.slice(2).map(guide => <a href={guide.href}><div><h4>{guide.name}</h4><p>{guide.description}</p></div><Icon name="external" size={17} /></a>)}</section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="developer-contribute">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Contributing</p><h2 id="developer-contribute">Work in the owning project.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="prose"><p>Report bugs and propose code changes in the affected project’s maintained repository. Include the version and the steps needed to reproduce a problem. Run that repository’s relevant checks and identify whether your evidence comes from automated tests, the emulator or a physical device.</p><p>For interface work, the <a href="/docs/design/pebble-ui-system/">shared Pebble UI standard</a> records the agreed watch and phone settings design. Alignment is pending; the current user guides describe released behaviour.</p><p>Website guides introduce the workflow; versioned library specifications remain authoritative for exact API fields, limits and wire formats. A library release does not update the dependency already bundled into an installed app.</p><p>Check the <a href="/docs/project/licensing/">project licences and source links</a> before reusing or contributing code. The current Pebble repositories use PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0.</p></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .build-guides > section > h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .build-guides h4 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: .9rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; font-weight: 550; }
  .build-guides a:hover h4 { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
</style>
